{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UkgvoDBDj25UtWBSnGZPmX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Experiment 6 Distinction-Inference Protocol — Session D-E6\n2\t\n3\tYou are **D-E6**, a decision-support session in a fresh, governed workspace\n4\tunder `contract.json` (K-E6-trial). Your workspace contains a raw task\n5\tpackage. Your job is **stage S1 of a topology pipeline**: infer, from raw\n6\ttask semantics alone, which unresolved distinctions matter, and estimate the\n7\tepistemic value of candidate execution organizations. You do **not** solve\n8\tthe task and you do **not** select a topology — selection is performed later\n9\tby a deterministic ranker outside your session.\n10\t\n11\tNothing outside this workspace is readable or writable. Your session grants\n12\tonly the tools **Read** and **Write**. You must not attempt to launch any\n13\tprocess, session, or agent.\n14\t\n15\t## Workspace layout\n16\t\n17\t```text\n18\tpackage/task.json                  the task: statement, deliverable spec, evidence requirements\n19\tpackage/artifacts/...              all task materials\n20\tcontract.json                      K-E6-trial (governing contract)\n21\tinfer-harness.json                 your declared HarnessSpec (4 nodes, linear)\n22\tdistinction-spec-schema.json       required shape of distinctions.json\n23\tvalue-estimates-schema.json        required shape of value-estimates.json\n24\tprotocol.md                        this file\n25\t```\n26\t\n27\t## What you produce\n28\t\n29\t### 1. `distinctions.json` (DistinctionSpec)\n30\t\n31\tThe unresolved distinctions of the task: the questions that must be settled,\n32\twith admissible evidence, for the deliverable to be verified. Follow\n33\t`distinction-spec-schema.json` exactly. 1–8 distinctions; use ids Q1, Q2, …\n34\t\n35\tFor each distinction:\n36\t- `question`: the precise unresolved question.\n37\t- `why_unresolved`: why the present evidence state does not settle it.\n38\t- `required_evidence`: what evidence would settle it.\n39\t- `admissibility_constraints`: conditions the evidence must satisfy to be\n40\t  admissible (quote or paraphrase the task's evidence requirements —\n41\t  especially any authorship/access conditions they impose).\n42\t- `evidence_requirement_refs`: which of the task's `evidence_requirements`\n43\t  ids (e.g. `E-A`) this distinction maps to. Every task evidence\n44\t  requirement must be referenced by at least one distinction.\n45\t- `dependencies`: distinction ids this one depends on.\n46\t- `features`: your **latent-structure inference**, the heart of this stage.\n47\t  All five booleans are required:\n48\t  - `locally_resolvable`: this session-shaped process, having read the\n49\t    package, could produce admissible evidence settling this distinction\n50\t    by itself.\n51\t  - `requires_isolation`: admissible evidence requires an origin that is\n52\t    causally separated from this process — for example authorship without\n53\t    access to a package artifact, a derivation that must not consult\n54\t    earlier work, a search or enumeration that must not be anchored on a\n55\t    prior answer, or a judgment that must not be influenced by the\n56\t    producer of the answer it judges.\n57\t  - `contamination`: reading the package has already destroyed this\n58\t    process's ability to produce that admissible evidence (you cannot\n59\t    un-see an artifact or un-anchor on an answer you have formed).\n60\t  - `capability_bearing_artifact`: resolving this distinction requires\n61\t    authoring an artifact that would grant execution capability\n62\t    (contracts, harnesses, prompts for other processes).\n63\t  - `spans_sessions`: resolution inherently spans process/session\n64\t    boundaries (state must survive a session death).\n65\t\n66\t  Judge features honestly from the task's own evidence requirements and\n67\t  admissibility conditions. Most tasks have most features false. A\n68\t  distinction can be `locally_resolvable=true` even if hard; difficulty is\n69\t  not the criterion — admissibility is.\n70\t\n71\t### 2. `value-estimates.json`\n72\t\n73\tPredicted observed-value components for each of the four candidate\n74\torganization families (schema: `value-estimates-schema.json`). These\n75\tpredictions are frozen and later compared against measured values, so\n76\testimate what will actually be observed, not what sounds safe.\n77\t\n78\tThe families (structure fixed by a closed grammar; you estimate value only):\n79\t\n80\t- `local`: one worker process (like this one) resolves everything and a\n81\t  deterministic root check verifies the deliverable. 1 model process.\n82\t- `local-independent-verify`: as `local`, plus a second, separately\n83\t  launched examiner process that re-derives/checks the answer against the\n84\t  package without being its author (it does see the answer). 2 model\n85\t  processes.\n86\t- `isolated-child`: the worker authors a bundle for one separately\n87\t  launched, causally isolated process whose inputs the worker chooses\n88\t  (it can exclude package artifacts and its own conclusions); a\n89\t  deterministic root step integrates the isolated process's output into\n90\t  the final deliverable. 2 model processes, 1 of them the isolated one.\n91\t- `branching`: the worker defers the choice between the `local` and\n92\t  `isolated-child` shapes to run time, then realizes exactly one branch.\n93\t  Costed at the `isolated-child` rate.\n94\t\n95\tFor each family estimate, per the operationalized measurement:\n96\t\n97\t- `delta_e` in [0,1]: the fraction of the task's `evidence_requirements`\n98\t  that the family will satisfy **with admissible evidence** (deterministic\n99\t  root verification decides satisfaction; evidence violating an\n100\t  admissibility/authorship condition does not count).\n101\t- `redundancy` in [0,1]: the expected fraction of evidence records that\n102\t  merely duplicate evidence the worker already had. A separate path whose\n103\t  output is REQUIRED for evidence admissibility produces novel records\n104\t  (redundancy near 0); a separate path that merely re-derives what the\n105\t  worker can fully establish produces duplicates (for example a\n106\t  confirming re-check of an already-verified answer, or an extra process\n107\t  on a task whose evidence requirements the worker alone satisfies).\n108\t- `governance_risk` in [0,1]: 0.25 × expected number of formal/governance\n109\t  failures (freshness, attenuation, refinement, observability). Every\n110\t  execution runs under deterministic governance machinery, so failures\n111\t  are rare: 0.0 is the right estimate unless you concretely expect a\n112\t  violation; 0.25 means you expect one actual failure. Do not use this\n113\t  component to encode vague caution — it is scored against the measured\n114\t  failure count.\n115\t- `rationale`: one or two sentences, externally inspectable.\n116\t\n117\tCost is **not** estimated: it is computed deterministically from the\n118\tfamily's process counts.\n119\t\n120\t## Ledger\n121\t\n122\tMaintain `execution-ledger.jsonl` in the workspace root, one JSON object\n123\tper line: `{\"event_id\", \"label\", \"actor\", \"timestamp\", \"artifact_refs\",\n124\t\"metadata\"}` following `infer-harness.json` → `ledger_contract` exactly.\n125\tFive node events in order (observe-package, infer-distinctions,\n126\testimate-value, self-check-spec, return-spec), each with\n127\t`metadata.completes_node`. Both JSON deliverables are capability-relevant\n128\tproposals: their authoring events use label `propose` with the file in\n129\t`artifact_refs`.\n130\t\n131\t## Conduct\n132\t\n133\t1. Execute `observe-package`: read everything in the workspace.\n134\t2. Execute `infer-distinctions`: write `distinctions.json`.\n135\t3. Execute `estimate-value`: write `value-estimates.json`.\n136\t4. Execute `self-check-spec`: re-read both artifacts against their schemas;\n137\t   record the outcome in the ledger (non-authoritative).\n138\t5. Execute `return-spec`: write `spec-summary.json` — `{\"task_id\": ...,\n139\t   \"distinction_count\": N, \"families_estimated\": 4}` — and finish the\n140\t   ledger. Do not emit a `complete` event; completion is recorded by the\n141\t   root lifecycle log.\n142\t\n143\tHonesty over confidence: your distinctions and estimates are scored against\n144\twhat later actually happens, not against how thorough they look.\n145\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97b645dc-872a-4bd1-b98d-a82aa7fede37","uuid":"a2172e29-5f84-453a-96fc-e3fd0c846a5f","timestamp":"2026-08-09T20:39:40.455Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/87cd2a2d-a4f9-585b-836f-2648df7a6284/scratchpad/e7run/A/e7-t02/infer-ws/protocol.md","content":"# Experiment 6 Distinction-Inference Protocol — Session D-E6\n\nYou are **D-E6**, a decision-support session in a fresh, governed workspace\nunder `contract.json` (K-E6-trial). Your workspace contains a raw task\npackage. Your job is **stage S1 of a topology pipeline**: infer, from raw\ntask semantics alone, which unresolved distinctions matter, and estimate the\nepistemic value of candidate execution organizations. You do **not** solve\nthe task and you do **not** select a topology — selection is performed later\nby a deterministic ranker outside your session.\n\nNothing outside this workspace is readable or writable. Your session grants\nonly the tools **Read** and **Write**. You must not attempt to launch any\nprocess, session, or agent.\n\n## Workspace layout\n\n```text\npackage/task.json                  the task: statement, deliverable spec, evidence requirements\npackage/artifacts/...              all task materials\ncontract.json                      K-E6-trial (governing contract)\ninfer-harness.json                 your declared HarnessSpec (4 nodes, linear)\ndistinction-spec-schema.json       required shape of distinctions.json\nvalue-estimates-schema.json        required shape of value-estimates.json\nprotocol.md                        this file\n```\n\n## What you produce\n\n### 1. `distinctions.json` (DistinctionSpec)\n\nThe unresolved distinctions of the task: the questions that must be settled,\nwith admissible evidence, for the deliverable to be verified. Follow\n`distinction-spec-schema.json` exactly. 1–8 distinctions; use ids Q1, Q2, …\n\nFor each distinction:\n- `question`: the precise unresolved question.\n- `why_unresolved`: why the present evidence state does not settle it.\n- `required_evidence`: what evidence would settle it.\n- `admissibility_constraints`: conditions the evidence must satisfy to be\n  admissible (quote or paraphrase the task's evidence requirements —\n  especially any authorship/access conditions they impose).\n- `evidence_requirement_refs`: which of the task's `evidence_requirements`\n  ids (e.g. `E-A`) this distinction maps to. Every task evidence\n  requirement must be referenced by at least one distinction.\n- `dependencies`: distinction ids this one depends on.\n- `features`: your **latent-structure inference**, the heart of this stage.\n  All five booleans are required:\n  - `locally_resolvable`: this session-shaped process, having read the\n    package, could produce admissible evidence settling this distinction\n    by itself.\n  - `requires_isolation`: admissible evidence requires an origin that is\n    causally separated from this process — for example authorship without\n    access to a package artifact, a derivation that must not consult\n    earlier work, a search or enumeration that must not be anchored on a\n    prior answer, or a judgment that must not be influenced by the\n    producer of the answer it judges.\n  - `contamination`: reading the package has already destroyed this\n    process's ability to produce that admissible evidence (you cannot\n    un-see an artifact or un-anchor on an answer you have formed).\n  - `capability_bearing_artifact`: resolving this distinction requires\n    authoring an artifact that would grant execution capability\n    (contracts, harnesses, prompts for other processes).\n  - `spans_sessions`: resolution inherently spans process/session\n    boundaries (state must survive a session death).\n\n  Judge features honestly from the task's own evidence requirements and\n  admissibility conditions. Most tasks have most features false. A\n  distinction can be `locally_resolvable=true` even if hard; difficulty is\n  not the criterion — admissibility is.\n\n### 2. `value-estimates.json`\n\nPredicted observed-value components for each of the four candidate\norganization families (schema: `value-estimates-schema.json`). These\npredictions are frozen and later compared against measured values, so\nestimate what will actually be observed, not what sounds safe.\n\nThe families (structure fixed by a closed grammar; you estimate value only):\n\n- `local`: one worker process (like this one) resolves everything and a\n  deterministic root check verifies the deliverable. 1 model process.\n- `local-independent-verify`: as `local`, plus a second, separately\n  launched examiner process that re-derives/checks the answer against the\n  package without being its author (it does see the answer). 2 model\n  processes.\n- `isolated-child`: the worker authors a bundle for one separately\n  launched, causally isolated process whose inputs the worker chooses\n  (it can exclude package artifacts and its own conclusions); a\n  deterministic root step integrates the isolated process's output into\n  the final deliverable. 2 model processes, 1 of them the isolated one.\n- `branching`: the worker defers the choice between the `local` and\n  `isolated-child` shapes to run time, then realizes exactly one branch.\n  Costed at the `isolated-child` rate.\n\nFor each family estimate, per the operationalized measurement:\n\n- `delta_e` in [0,1]: the fraction of the task's `evidence_requirements`\n  that the family will satisfy **with admissible evidence** (deterministic\n  root verification decides satisfaction; evidence violating an\n  admissibility/authorship condition does not count).\n- `redundancy` in [0,1]: the expected fraction of evidence records that\n  merely duplicate evidence the worker already had. A separate path whose\n  output is REQUIRED for evidence admissibility produces novel records\n  (redundancy near 0); a separate path that merely re-derives what the\n  worker can fully establish produces duplicates (for example a\n  confirming re-check of an already-verified answer, or an extra process\n  on a task whose evidence requirements the worker alone satisfies).\n- `governance_risk` in [0,1]: 0.25 × expected number of formal/governance\n  failures (freshness, attenuation, refinement, observability). Every\n  execution runs under deterministic governance machinery, so failures\n  are rare: 0.0 is the right estimate unless you concretely expect a\n  violation; 0.25 means you expect one actual failure. Do not use this\n  component to encode vague caution — it is scored against the measured\n  failure count.\n- `rationale`: one or two sentences, externally inspectable.\n\nCost is **not** estimated: it is computed deterministically from the\nfamily's process counts.\n\n## Ledger\n\nMaintain `execution-ledger.jsonl` in the workspace root, one JSON object\nper line: `{\"event_id\", \"label\", \"actor\", \"timestamp\", \"artifact_refs\",\n\"metadata\"}` following `infer-harness.json` → `ledger_contract` exactly.\nFive node events in order (observe-package, infer-distinctions,\nestimate-value, self-check-spec, return-spec), each with\n`metadata.completes_node`. Both JSON deliverables are capability-relevant\nproposals: their authoring events use label `propose` with the file in\n`artifact_refs`.\n\n## Conduct\n\n1. Execute `observe-package`: read everything in the workspace.\n2. Execute `infer-distinctions`: write `distinctions.json`.\n3. Execute `estimate-value`: write `value-estimates.json`.\n4. Execute `self-check-spec`: re-read both artifacts against their schemas;\n   record the outcome in the ledger (non-authoritative).\n5. Execute `return-spec`: write `spec-summary.json` — `{\"task_id\": ...,\n   \"distinction_count\": N, \"families_estimated\": 4}` — and finish the\n   ledger. Do not emit a `complete` event; completion is recorded by the\n   root lifecycle log.\n\nHonesty over confidence: your distinctions and estimates are scored against\nwhat later actually happens, not against how thorough they look.\n","numLines":145,"startLine":1,"totalLines":145}}}
