{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015bo3JfRGCVM9eCg7V8pShM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"task_id\": \"e7-t02\",\n3\t  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n4\t    {\n5\t      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n6\t      \"question\": \"Which classes of inputs in the stated domain (lists of at most 6 integer intervals with endpoints in [-10, 10], start <= end) could the truth of the claim turn on — for example intervals that touch at a shared boundary (previous end == next start), nested intervals, duplicate intervals, zero-length intervals (start == end), the empty list, and single-interval lists?\",\n7\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"The package contains only the claim text and the source of merge.py; no analysis of the input space exists yet, so no party has identified which structural classes interact with merge.py's comparison `s < out[-1][1]` and its max-extension logic.\",\n8\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A written analysis enumerating the candidate input classes, tied to the specific branch conditions and merge logic of merge.py, showing on which classes the claim's pairwise no-overlap condition could plausibly fail or must hold.\",\n9\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n10\t        \"The analysis must cover the stated domain (<= 6 intervals, integer endpoints in [-10, 10], start <= end) and not a different domain.\",\n11\t        \"Per E-A, it must identify the input classes on which the claim's truth could turn, not merely list arbitrary test categories.\"\n12\t      ],\n13\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"],\n14\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n15\t      \"features\": {\n16\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n17\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n18\t        \"contamination\": false,\n19\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n20\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n21\t      }\n22\t    },\n23\t    {\n24\t      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n25\t      \"question\": \"Does merge(intervals) as implemented satisfy the claim over the entire stated domain (HOLDS), or does some in-domain input yield an output that, after sorting, contains two intervals i before j with i's end >= j's start (VIOLATED) — and if VIOLATED, what concrete input demonstrates it?\",\n26\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"Only the source code is available; no execution trace, exhaustive check, or whole-domain argument has been recorded, so the verdict and any concrete violating input are not yet established.\",\n27\t      \"required_evidence\": \"Either a concrete in-domain input together with a mechanical trace of merge on that input showing the output violates the pairwise condition, or a domain-covering argument that no such input exists.\",\n28\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n29\t        \"A violating input must lie inside the stated domain: at most 6 intervals, integer endpoints in [-10, 10], start <= end for each interval.\",\n30\t        \"Per E-C, the violation must be mechanical: the claimed violating input's merged-and-sorted output must exhibit a concrete pair i before j with end_i >= start_j.\",\n31\t        \"The deliverable result.json must carry the verdict, the violating input (or null on HOLDS), and the input classes examined.\"\n32\t      ],\n33\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-C\"],\n34\t      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\"],\n35\t      \"features\": {\n36\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n37\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n38\t        \"contamination\": false,\n39\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n40\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n41\t      }\n42\t    },\n43\t    {\n44\t      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n45\t      \"question\": \"Has a systematic search of the stated domain for a violating input been carried out by a party other than the author of the provisional answer, or has such a non-author party produced an argument that no violating input exists in the domain?\",\n46\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"No record from any second party exists in the package, and any search performed by the same process that authored the provisional verdict is inadmissible under E-B's authorship condition, so the requirement is unmet regardless of how thorough the author's own search is.\",\n47\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A search or enumeration record over the stated domain (or a nonexistence argument covering it) authored by a process that is not the author of the provisional answer, delivered in a form the root can integrate into the final deliverable's evidence.\",\n48\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n49\t        \"E-B's authorship condition: the search (or nonexistence argument) must be 'carried out by a party other than the author of the provisional answer'.\",\n50\t        \"The search must be systematic over the stated domain, not a spot check of the author's proposed counterexample.\",\n51\t        \"The searching party should derive its result from the task materials rather than being anchored on the provisional answer as its starting point.\"\n52\t      ],\n53\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"],\n54\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n55\t      \"features\": {\n56\t        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n57\t        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n58\t        \"contamination\": true,\n59\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n60\t        \"spans_sessions\": true\n61\t      }\n62\t    }\n63\t  ]\n64\t}\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97b645dc-872a-4bd1-b98d-a82aa7fede37","uuid":"ec489306-eb17-421e-aa01-ffc9241fc694","timestamp":"2026-08-09T20:42:01.279Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/87cd2a2d-a4f9-585b-836f-2648df7a6284/scratchpad/e7run/A/e7-t02/infer-ws/distinctions.json","content":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"e7-t02\",\n  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"question\": \"Which classes of inputs in the stated domain (lists of at most 6 integer intervals with endpoints in [-10, 10], start <= end) could the truth of the claim turn on — for example intervals that touch at a shared boundary (previous end == next start), nested intervals, duplicate intervals, zero-length intervals (start == end), the empty list, and single-interval lists?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"The package contains only the claim text and the source of merge.py; no analysis of the input space exists yet, so no party has identified which structural classes interact with merge.py's comparison `s < out[-1][1]` and its max-extension logic.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A written analysis enumerating the candidate input classes, tied to the specific branch conditions and merge logic of merge.py, showing on which classes the claim's pairwise no-overlap condition could plausibly fail or must hold.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"The analysis must cover the stated domain (<= 6 intervals, integer endpoints in [-10, 10], start <= end) and not a different domain.\",\n        \"Per E-A, it must identify the input classes on which the claim's truth could turn, not merely list arbitrary test categories.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-A\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"question\": \"Does merge(intervals) as implemented satisfy the claim over the entire stated domain (HOLDS), or does some in-domain input yield an output that, after sorting, contains two intervals i before j with i's end >= j's start (VIOLATED) — and if VIOLATED, what concrete input demonstrates it?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"Only the source code is available; no execution trace, exhaustive check, or whole-domain argument has been recorded, so the verdict and any concrete violating input are not yet established.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"Either a concrete in-domain input together with a mechanical trace of merge on that input showing the output violates the pairwise condition, or a domain-covering argument that no such input exists.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"A violating input must lie inside the stated domain: at most 6 intervals, integer endpoints in [-10, 10], start <= end for each interval.\",\n        \"Per E-C, the violation must be mechanical: the claimed violating input's merged-and-sorted output must exhibit a concrete pair i before j with end_i >= start_j.\",\n        \"The deliverable result.json must carry the verdict, the violating input (or null on HOLDS), and the input classes examined.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-C\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [\"Q1\"],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Has a systematic search of the stated domain for a violating input been carried out by a party other than the author of the provisional answer, or has such a non-author party produced an argument that no violating input exists in the domain?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No record from any second party exists in the package, and any search performed by the same process that authored the provisional verdict is inadmissible under E-B's authorship condition, so the requirement is unmet regardless of how thorough the author's own search is.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A search or enumeration record over the stated domain (or a nonexistence argument covering it) authored by a process that is not the author of the provisional answer, delivered in a form the root can integrate into the final deliverable's evidence.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"E-B's authorship condition: the search (or nonexistence argument) must be 'carried out by a party other than the author of the provisional answer'.\",\n        \"The search must be systematic over the stated domain, not a spot check of the author's proposed counterexample.\",\n        \"The searching party should derive its result from the task materials rather than being anchored on the provisional answer as its starting point.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n        \"contamination\": true,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": true\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","numLines":65,"startLine":1,"totalLines":65}}}
